WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.626 --> 00:00:03.712
As the pandemic descended
on the world in 2020,

00:00:03.712 --> 00:00:07.132
people needed some outlet
to get out of the house.

00:00:07.132 --> 00:00:08.633
To be around friends,

00:00:08.633 --> 00:00:10.510
maybe even get in some light exercise

00:00:10.510 --> 00:00:13.221
while not risking spreading Covid.

00:00:13.221 --> 00:00:15.890
One sport checks all of those boxes

00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:19.519
and that is golf

00:00:19.519 --> 00:00:22.272
and to call it a resurgence
would be an understatement.

00:00:23.231 --> 00:00:27.027
As we went through 2020
and the world shut down,

00:00:27.027 --> 00:00:30.780
we went from concerned about solvency

00:00:30.780 --> 00:00:32.157
and when we're gonna open

00:00:32.157 --> 00:00:33.950
and if people are gonna be playing golf,

00:00:33.950 --> 00:00:37.537
to the largest golf boom that
I've ever been a part of.

00:00:37.537 --> 00:00:40.040
According to the National
Golf Foundation, in 2020,

00:00:40.040 --> 00:00:43.835
there were 24.8 million
golfers in the United States.

00:00:43.835 --> 00:00:48.757
An increase of about
500,000 and 2% over 2019,

00:00:48.757 --> 00:00:51.885
the largest net increase in 17 years.

00:00:51.885 --> 00:00:53.386
Golf's popularity right now

00:00:53.386 --> 00:00:55.638
has only one comparison in the past.

00:00:56.681 --> 00:00:58.308
For Tiger Woods for the first time.

00:00:58.308 --> 00:01:01.853
Tiger, who was amazing, but
his star burned very bright

00:01:01.853 --> 00:01:05.607
and then it didn't have
as strong a lasting power.

00:01:05.607 --> 00:01:07.942
But that's normal for a
unique athlete, right?

00:01:07.942 --> 00:01:10.528
They go through those phases,

00:01:10.528 --> 00:01:12.447
as opposed to what we're seeing right now,

00:01:12.447 --> 00:01:14.240
which is some structural change

00:01:14.240 --> 00:01:16.910
along with what is
candidly a Covid dividend.

00:01:17.786 --> 00:01:19.496
But it's more than just the pandemic

00:01:19.496 --> 00:01:21.706
that has made golf's popularity.

00:01:21.706 --> 00:01:25.126
It's also sweeping changes
to the game itself.

00:01:25.126 --> 00:01:26.836
There are cultural aspects of golf

00:01:26.836 --> 00:01:29.339
that I would say historically
did not make it friendly.

00:01:29.339 --> 00:01:32.300
I would say I think that is
changing dramatically now.

00:01:32.300 --> 00:01:33.802
It is becoming inclusive

00:01:33.802 --> 00:01:35.512
in the sense that everybody's welcome.

00:01:35.512 --> 00:01:37.180
Golf is becoming cooler.

00:01:37.180 --> 00:01:39.599
The mystique of like, what is a golfer,

00:01:39.599 --> 00:01:42.560
is becoming more and
more of, a golfer is me.

00:01:42.560 --> 00:01:44.437
A golfer could be anyone.

00:01:44.437 --> 00:01:46.898
In addition, there are
companies and technologies

00:01:46.898 --> 00:01:49.067
emerging both on and off the course

00:01:49.067 --> 00:01:50.902
that are making the game more accessible,

00:01:50.902 --> 00:01:52.153
making players better

00:01:52.153 --> 00:01:54.864
and diversifying who
decides to play the sport.

00:01:54.864 --> 00:01:56.074
Yeah.
Good contact.

00:01:56.074 --> 00:01:57.951
There's 80 million golfers in the world.

00:01:57.951 --> 00:02:01.079
Of that, I would say
probably 50 to 60 million

00:02:01.079 --> 00:02:02.247
are looking to get better.

00:02:02.247 --> 00:02:04.541
For anybody who's looking
to get better, it's for you

00:02:04.541 --> 00:02:06.251
and they've created features within there

00:02:06.251 --> 00:02:07.418
that help you target it.

00:02:07.418 --> 00:02:10.755
But can this popularity be
sustained for the long haul?

00:02:10.755 --> 00:02:12.632
That's what I'm about to find out.

00:02:12.632 --> 00:02:14.968
This is the future of golf

00:02:14.968 --> 00:02:16.553
and the question on the
minds of stakeholders

00:02:16.553 --> 00:02:19.681
around the globe is one of
reinvention and momentum.

00:02:19.681 --> 00:02:22.892
Can the age-old game of golf
convert its momentary success

00:02:22.892 --> 00:02:24.144
into permanent gains?

00:02:32.485 --> 00:02:34.195
So here's the thing about golf.

00:02:34.195 --> 00:02:37.991
It's hard, it's expensive,
and it's intimidating

00:02:37.991 --> 00:02:39.701
and in a place like New York City,

00:02:39.701 --> 00:02:41.536
it's really hard to find a real course

00:02:41.536 --> 00:02:43.621
that you can actually get access to.

00:02:43.621 --> 00:02:45.915
But there is one place
that's starting to figure out

00:02:45.915 --> 00:02:47.542
a couple of those challenges.

00:02:47.542 --> 00:02:51.296
First, the space, and second,
the intimidation factor

00:02:51.296 --> 00:02:53.339
and you don't have to worry about being

00:02:53.339 --> 00:02:55.842
as terrible as someone like me.

00:02:55.842 --> 00:02:57.302
You may have seen this pop up

00:02:57.302 --> 00:02:59.179
on your TikTok or Instagram feeds,

00:02:59.179 --> 00:03:01.973
people taking videos of themselves here.

00:03:01.973 --> 00:03:03.349
It's a place called Topgolf.

00:03:10.190 --> 00:03:14.652
Topgolf is the avenue
for most of the world

00:03:14.652 --> 00:03:17.322
to experience golf and get into golf

00:03:17.322 --> 00:03:21.701
and it never existed
back in the early 2000s.

00:03:21.701 --> 00:03:23.328
That's Chip Brewer, the CEO of Callaway,

00:03:23.328 --> 00:03:25.997
which bought Topgolf in March of 2021.

00:03:28.458 --> 00:03:30.585
Topgolf is like if a
driving range, an arcade,

00:03:30.585 --> 00:03:32.503
and a bowling alley had a baby

00:03:32.503 --> 00:03:35.048
and it's the leading
off-course golf experience

00:03:35.048 --> 00:03:35.882
in the world.

00:03:37.008 --> 00:03:39.677
Well, on-course golf is what you
think traditional golf.

00:03:39.677 --> 00:03:42.430
So there's 24 million people in the U.S.

00:03:42.430 --> 00:03:45.892
that play golf on a golf course per year.

00:03:45.892 --> 00:03:48.436
But most of those play one round.

00:03:48.436 --> 00:03:52.106
Okay so, and then
off-course golf means that

00:03:52.106 --> 00:03:55.735
you experience golf not on
a green grass golf course.

00:03:55.735 --> 00:03:59.489
So that is you're going to a
Topgolf or a driving range.

00:04:00.365 --> 00:04:02.283
There are currently 70 Topgolf locations

00:04:02.283 --> 00:04:04.452
around the world today
and it's growing fast,

00:04:04.452 --> 00:04:07.538
with the biggest Topgolf
ever slated to open in China.

00:04:08.998 --> 00:04:10.792
So we don't hand you a rule book.

00:04:10.792 --> 00:04:13.169
We hand you immediate pathway to fun

00:04:13.169 --> 00:04:15.505
and having a good time
with people you care about.

00:04:15.505 --> 00:04:17.966
This is Artie Starrs, the CEO of Topgolf.

00:04:19.133 --> 00:04:20.510
Artie, tell me about your customer,

00:04:20.510 --> 00:04:22.303
because as they come through Topgolf,

00:04:22.303 --> 00:04:24.472
it's not just folks who
look like you and me.

00:04:24.472 --> 00:04:27.141
So when we look at our venue business,

00:04:27.141 --> 00:04:29.894
we think everyone is a potential guest,

00:04:29.894 --> 00:04:31.354
a potential customer.

00:04:31.354 --> 00:04:34.065
Since traditional golf
skews old and white,

00:04:34.065 --> 00:04:36.317
Topgolf's gamification of
the driving range appeals to

00:04:36.317 --> 00:04:38.361
a younger, more diverse crowd.

00:04:38.361 --> 00:04:40.863
People who might not
otherwise even think about

00:04:40.863 --> 00:04:41.948
picking up a club.

00:04:44.075 --> 00:04:46.244
You would see families, you
would see different ages.

00:04:46.244 --> 00:04:47.328
You would see different backgrounds,

00:04:47.328 --> 00:04:48.871
different income brackets.

00:04:48.871 --> 00:04:50.915
People who have never played golf before

00:04:50.915 --> 00:04:52.083
and people who play a lot.

00:04:52.083 --> 00:04:54.752
If you came to one of our
venues, you would see that.

00:04:56.296 --> 00:04:58.047
People with all sorts of backgrounds,

00:04:58.047 --> 00:05:01.050
all sorts of golf experience,
non-golf experience.

00:05:01.050 --> 00:05:04.012
We have over 70 venues
in the U.S. right now,

00:05:04.012 --> 00:05:07.056
approximately 500,000 guests per venue,

00:05:07.056 --> 00:05:10.977
so 35 million experiences
that we have every year.

00:05:10.977 --> 00:05:13.062
However, there are aspects to Topgolf

00:05:13.062 --> 00:05:15.148
that appeal to more serious golfers

00:05:15.148 --> 00:05:17.650
and that's its technology
called Toptracer,

00:05:17.650 --> 00:05:19.319
which gives the customer more information

00:05:19.319 --> 00:05:22.572
on the distance, height,
and speed of their drives.

00:05:22.572 --> 00:05:24.157
Our Toptracer business,

00:05:24.157 --> 00:05:26.576
that tends to cater a bit more to people

00:05:26.576 --> 00:05:28.578
who are trying to get better at golf,

00:05:28.578 --> 00:05:31.205
and might spend a couple
hours at a driving range

00:05:31.205 --> 00:05:32.707
and stay engaged in our app.

00:05:32.707 --> 00:05:34.459
When I grew up taking golf lessons,

00:05:34.459 --> 00:05:35.918
it was very much a,

00:05:35.918 --> 00:05:39.088
lick your finger, okay, make
your swing a little bit better.

00:05:39.088 --> 00:05:40.590
Now we give you an app.

00:05:40.590 --> 00:05:44.969
We tell you how far and high
and fast your ball is going.

00:05:44.969 --> 00:05:47.680
We give you exercises
and actual things to do.

00:05:47.680 --> 00:05:49.390
We do this at Topgolf as well.

00:05:49.390 --> 00:05:51.434
When it comes to the
popularity of Topgolf,

00:05:51.434 --> 00:05:53.394
it's a rising tide that lifts all boats

00:05:53.394 --> 00:05:55.980
for both Topgolf and Callaway.

00:05:55.980 --> 00:05:59.108
I think for people that
are coming in and playing

00:05:59.108 --> 00:06:02.612
for their first time or for
their first time in a while,

00:06:02.612 --> 00:06:05.782
we're a place that can remind guests

00:06:05.782 --> 00:06:07.909
of the thrill of hitting a ball

00:06:07.909 --> 00:06:10.161
and having fun with a
golf club in your hand.

00:06:12.330 --> 00:06:14.874
Topgolf is changing the world of golf

00:06:14.874 --> 00:06:19.879
and it's creating access
to players of all types.

00:06:20.338 --> 00:06:24.300
By merging the two, we have
a competitive advantage

00:06:24.300 --> 00:06:28.179
in overall reach to
golfers of all abilities

00:06:28.179 --> 00:06:31.057
and you think about growth of the sport,

00:06:31.057 --> 00:06:32.892
but then growth of our business.

00:06:36.062 --> 00:06:38.272
One of the biggest reasons
people don't stick to golf

00:06:38.272 --> 00:06:40.817
is because it's hard.

00:06:40.817 --> 00:06:44.070
As the famous quote goes,
golf is a good walk spoiled.

00:06:44.070 --> 00:06:47.740
But Sal Syed, the CEO of
Arccos, is out to change that.

00:06:51.994 --> 00:06:54.831
So now we're on like a short par 4.

00:06:54.831 --> 00:06:56.749
For the reward that you're looking for.

00:07:02.588 --> 00:07:06.259
So you're a data guy, analytics,
go to business school.

00:07:06.259 --> 00:07:09.178
You get this idea, and
the idea turns out to be

00:07:09.178 --> 00:07:10.596
a golf tech company.

00:07:10.596 --> 00:07:11.389
How, why?

00:07:11.389 --> 00:07:12.223
Tell me the story.

00:07:12.223 --> 00:07:14.851
We realized that there was literally

00:07:14.851 --> 00:07:16.686
nobody touching data in golf

00:07:16.686 --> 00:07:17.979
and golf's a huge industry,

00:07:17.979 --> 00:07:21.232
like 90, a hundred billion
dollars spent every year on golf

00:07:21.232 --> 00:07:24.777
and the entire reason
for existence of a golfer

00:07:24.777 --> 00:07:26.529
is to get better at golf

00:07:26.529 --> 00:07:29.949
and that improvement ends
up showing as your score.

00:07:29.949 --> 00:07:32.034
But that score is composed
of so many different things.

00:07:32.034 --> 00:07:34.537
So many different shots that
are taken, how they're taken

00:07:34.537 --> 00:07:36.914
and we realized that we need to track

00:07:36.914 --> 00:07:38.916
every shot that's being
taken on the golf course,

00:07:38.916 --> 00:07:41.252
to then analyze correctly

00:07:41.252 --> 00:07:43.296
where your strengths and weaknesses lie.

00:07:43.296 --> 00:07:47.133
Wind is kind of coming this
way, eight miles an hour,

00:07:47.133 --> 00:07:49.427
actual is 86, playing like 87.

00:07:49.427 --> 00:07:50.928
So that's what we're gonna do.

00:07:55.016 --> 00:07:58.102
In the most basic terms, how does it work?

00:07:58.102 --> 00:07:59.061
The way it works is

00:07:59.061 --> 00:08:00.188
there's a one-time pairing process.

00:08:00.188 --> 00:08:03.524
So these sensors, think of them
as impact detection sensors.

00:08:03.524 --> 00:08:05.359
So they're detecting
whenever you make impact

00:08:05.359 --> 00:08:06.194
with the golf ball.

00:08:06.194 --> 00:08:07.820
When it's paired with your smartphone,

00:08:07.820 --> 00:08:11.032
so we're basically dropping
pins, every shot you take

00:08:11.032 --> 00:08:12.909
and we're recording a bunch
of information around it,

00:08:12.909 --> 00:08:14.994
what club was used, what was the terrain.

00:08:14.994 --> 00:08:17.413
Was it, you started at the tee,
ended up in the left rough.

00:08:17.413 --> 00:08:19.165
How far in the left rough was it?

00:08:19.165 --> 00:08:20.249
What were the weather conditions?

00:08:20.249 --> 00:08:22.126
What direction was the wind going?

00:08:22.126 --> 00:08:23.044
Was it sunny or not?

00:08:23.044 --> 00:08:23.878
Was it cloudy or not?

00:08:23.878 --> 00:08:26.255
Like all those different things factor in

00:08:26.255 --> 00:08:28.007
and then we're able to analyze your game.

00:08:28.007 --> 00:08:30.134
But very simply, we're
recording every shot

00:08:30.134 --> 00:08:32.428
and then giving you insights about

00:08:32.428 --> 00:08:33.846
what your strengths and weaknesses are.

00:08:45.816 --> 00:08:48.528
So use this to help me understand

00:08:48.528 --> 00:08:51.197
how this technology would
help me as a putter.

00:08:51.197 --> 00:08:53.074
This is one of the widest greens in golf.

00:08:53.074 --> 00:08:55.743
It has a five foot swale
that you gotta traverse

00:08:55.743 --> 00:08:59.580
and I have, looking at
like a 55 foot putt

00:08:59.580 --> 00:09:01.624
and for me to get better at this course,

00:09:01.624 --> 00:09:03.668
I knew I was gonna have
enough 50 plus foot putts

00:09:03.668 --> 00:09:05.127
that I need to improve
that part of my game.

00:09:05.127 --> 00:09:07.797
So the app highlighted, you
know, my 0 to 10 feet's good.

00:09:07.797 --> 00:09:09.590
I'm grading a lot of those.

00:09:09.590 --> 00:09:11.926
10 to 25, 25 to 50, no problem.

00:09:11.926 --> 00:09:13.803
It's 50 plus, that
whenever I'm getting there,

00:09:13.803 --> 00:09:14.637
I was in trouble.

00:09:14.637 --> 00:09:16.013
So I started practicing lag putts,

00:09:16.013 --> 00:09:19.225
like look at this putt,
this is like 60 feet.

00:09:19.225 --> 00:09:21.561
It helped me target my putting practice

00:09:21.561 --> 00:09:23.604
to the exact area which was my weakness,

00:09:23.604 --> 00:09:24.939
which was 50 plus feet.

00:09:24.939 --> 00:09:26.482
Prior to that, you just knew,

00:09:26.482 --> 00:09:28.317
I'm three-putting a lot, or I'm-

00:09:28.317 --> 00:09:29.569
Yeah, exactly.

00:09:29.569 --> 00:09:31.988
And if you know you're
three-putting a lot,

00:09:31.988 --> 00:09:34.532
it could be that you're,

00:09:34.532 --> 00:09:36.325
like, you don't know what range
you're three-putting from.

00:09:36.325 --> 00:09:37.785
That's really, really important context

00:09:37.785 --> 00:09:39.078
and so when we track that,

00:09:39.078 --> 00:09:40.705
we're able to then take all that data,

00:09:40.705 --> 00:09:42.790
over the course of a round or five rounds

00:09:42.790 --> 00:09:45.918
and really show you that
this is not an anomaly.

00:09:45.918 --> 00:09:47.587
This is really where your issue lies

00:09:47.587 --> 00:09:49.338
and that's really, really important.

00:09:49.338 --> 00:09:51.048
Do you wanna take it or
do you want me to take it?

00:09:51.048 --> 00:09:51.882
I'm gonna take it.

00:09:51.882 --> 00:09:53.175
Yeah, let's see it.

00:09:53.175 --> 00:09:54.719
You wanna go just a hair left of it,

00:09:54.719 --> 00:09:56.012
like a foot left of it.

00:09:56.012 --> 00:09:58.055
This is like, this is the craziest,

00:09:58.055 --> 00:10:02.351
this is almost like
miniature golf on steroids.

00:10:02.351 --> 00:10:03.644
Right?

00:10:03.644 --> 00:10:05.396
I don't even know what to do here.

00:10:05.396 --> 00:10:07.773
This is from like a famous hole in France.

00:10:07.773 --> 00:10:10.276
It was called the Chasm Hole in Biarritz.

00:10:11.777 --> 00:10:12.612
That's good.

00:10:13.571 --> 00:10:15.197
Go in the cup!

00:10:15.197 --> 00:10:16.699
Ooh.

00:10:16.699 --> 00:10:19.368
There's a way to look
at this interestingly

00:10:19.368 --> 00:10:21.454
and I want you to break this down for me,

00:10:21.454 --> 00:10:22.288
where you look at this like,

00:10:22.288 --> 00:10:24.206
well, this is really only
for really good golfers.

00:10:24.206 --> 00:10:26.667
Like who can understand the data,

00:10:26.667 --> 00:10:28.502
who can sort of take this in.

00:10:28.502 --> 00:10:31.464
But then I can make the
case, this notion of like,

00:10:31.464 --> 00:10:34.425
actually this is for
really crappy golfers.

00:10:34.425 --> 00:10:35.384
I mean, it's a fair question.

00:10:35.384 --> 00:10:37.094
In fact, it seems like it's for everybody,

00:10:37.094 --> 00:10:39.221
but I want you to help me understand like,

00:10:39.221 --> 00:10:40.389
who gets what from this?

00:10:40.389 --> 00:10:42.725
Yeah, we cater to every type of golfer.

00:10:42.725 --> 00:10:44.727
It'll take your dispersion
patterns into account,

00:10:44.727 --> 00:10:46.979
it'll take the hazards into
account, the wind conditions

00:10:46.979 --> 00:10:49.815
and tell you for each shot,
what your optimal club is.

00:10:49.815 --> 00:10:52.985
What Arccos does is it takes
that cognitive bias away

00:10:52.985 --> 00:10:56.572
and it's able to, for the
average golfer out there,

00:10:56.572 --> 00:10:58.949
really help them understand
how far their clubs go.

00:10:58.949 --> 00:11:01.577
So give me the numbers here,
like in terms of growth

00:11:01.577 --> 00:11:03.412
and this is all about data

00:11:03.412 --> 00:11:06.749
and ever bigger numbers
mean better data, right?

00:11:06.749 --> 00:11:07.375
I mean-

00:11:07.375 --> 00:11:10.086
To date, we've recorded 500 million shots.

00:11:10.086 --> 00:11:13.214
Like in the future, playing without Arccos

00:11:13.214 --> 00:11:15.549
or a technology like it, as a golfer,

00:11:15.549 --> 00:11:18.469
will be akin to playing without a putter.

00:11:18.469 --> 00:11:21.180
You'll literally be leaving
strokes on the table

00:11:21.180 --> 00:11:25.518
and so I think this will
become like, a mainstay.

00:11:25.518 --> 00:11:27.645
I think that's the evolution of this

00:11:27.645 --> 00:11:30.398
sport and any sport,
and any industry, honestly.

00:11:30.398 --> 00:11:32.983
Ultimately, in order for golf
to maintain its momentum,

00:11:32.983 --> 00:11:35.945
it needs companies like
Callaway, Arccos, Topgolf,

00:11:35.945 --> 00:11:37.613
and even the PGA itself,

00:11:37.613 --> 00:11:39.990
to continue to emphasize the importance

00:11:39.990 --> 00:11:42.159
of including a younger,
more diverse demographic

00:11:42.159 --> 00:11:43.619
to play the game.

00:11:43.619 --> 00:11:48.290
Golf has needed, I dare
say, for a number of years,

00:11:48.290 --> 00:11:51.502
a little bit of a reboot
or a recasting of itself,

00:11:51.502 --> 00:11:52.628
literally and figuratively,

00:11:52.628 --> 00:11:55.005
because this is a demographic

00:11:55.005 --> 00:11:57.425
that the traditional demographic golf,

00:11:57.425 --> 00:11:59.760
is getting older year by year.

00:11:59.760 --> 00:12:01.846
Do you feel that happening?

00:12:01.846 --> 00:12:03.973
I would say the racial barriers of golf

00:12:03.973 --> 00:12:05.266
are withering away.

00:12:05.266 --> 00:12:08.018
I think the economic
barriers are still there.

00:12:08.018 --> 00:12:09.812
Golf as an industry is realizing that

00:12:09.812 --> 00:12:11.981
it's important to be inclusive.

00:12:11.981 --> 00:12:15.484
But we need to, every single year,

00:12:15.484 --> 00:12:18.070
open it up a little bit more.

00:12:18.070 --> 00:12:19.864
Making the game easier to play,

00:12:19.864 --> 00:12:21.866
making the rules on green grass

00:12:21.866 --> 00:12:23.993
simpler and simpler to understand.

00:12:23.993 --> 00:12:26.829
Providing more forums for competition.

00:12:26.829 --> 00:12:29.039
We always think that we are going,

00:12:29.039 --> 00:12:31.208
we are pushing the envelope forward,

00:12:31.208 --> 00:12:33.002
in terms of making golf more accessible.

00:12:33.002 --> 00:12:35.546
Because this technology is
designed for beginners as well.

00:12:35.546 --> 00:12:37.214
There are a bunch of people who,

00:12:37.214 --> 00:12:38.924
when you're starting
golf, it's a little scary.

00:12:38.924 --> 00:12:41.010
You don't know what
club to hit, what to do

00:12:41.010 --> 00:12:42.303
and so we make it easier.

00:12:42.303 --> 00:12:43.137
We make it easier

00:12:43.137 --> 00:12:44.930
and then a huge win,
not just for the sport,

00:12:44.930 --> 00:12:46.682
but for the people that
it'll be accessible to,

00:12:46.682 --> 00:12:49.101
'cause I do believe that
it's the greatest sport.

